# Paths left out of the OpenSearch core cache key (build-scripts/cache/cache-key.sh).
#
# One git pathspec per line, with glob magic: "*" stays within a directory, "**" crosses
# directories. Everything that is not listed here is part of the key, so a new file is a
# key input until someone proves otherwise: a missing entry costs a cache miss, a wrong
# one ships a stale core. core.include brings back files that a broader line here drops.
#
# Each entry was checked against the min package (see build-scripts/cache/README.md):
# changing the file leaves the Gradle output unchanged, or the assembly takes the file
# from the repository instead of from the min package.

# Repository tooling and documentation. README.md is bundled in the packages and stays in.
# .gitignore is not read by the build; what it ignores is left out of the key anyway.
.gitignore
.github/**
.idea/**
build-scripts/**
tools/**
.lychee.excludes
.whitesource
whitesource.config
codecov.yml
Vagrantfile
ADMINS.md
AGENTS.md
CHANGELOG.md
CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md
CONTRIBUTING.md
DEVELOPER_GUIDE.md
MAINTAINERS.md
PERFORMANCE_BENCHMARKS.md
RELEASING.md
SECURITY.md
TESTING.md
TRIAGING.md

# Package metadata and scripts that assemble.sh reads from the repository. The min deb
# carries its own maintainer scripts, but the assembly extracts only its data.tar.gz.
distribution/packages/src/rpm/**
distribution/packages/src/deb/debian/**
distribution/packages/src/deb/Makefile
distribution/packages/src/deb/debmake_install.sh
distribution/src/lib/**

# Bundled in the min package, but assemble.sh reads them from the repository.
distribution/src/config/opensearch.prod.yml
distribution/src/config/security/*.wazuh.yml

# Only its "version" field reaches the core (through product_version.sh); cache-key.sh
# adds it on its own. The bundled copy is regenerated by assemble.sh.
VERSION.json
